const __blk0=staticBlock(staticMarkup(' <section> <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Live Demo</h2> <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll the box below. The toolbar sticks to the top of the scroll container, and <code>pdx-change</code> says so.</p> <p class="pdx-txt-small affix-state" aria-live="polite">Affixed: <strong><!----></strong></p> <div class="scroll-container" id="affix-container"> <div class="scroll-spacer"> <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll down to see the toolbar become sticky.</p> </div> <pdx-affix target="#affix-container"> <div class="sticky-bar" data-pdx-u4xb1z-in> <pdx-icon name="filter" size="16" data-pdx-u4xb1z-in></pdx-icon> <strong data-pdx-u4xb1z-in>Sticky Toolbar</strong> <span class="pdx-ink-muted" data-pdx-u4xb1z-in>— scrolls with content, then sticks</span> </div> </pdx-affix> <div class="scroll-content"> <p>This content scrolls normally beneath the sticky toolbar.</p> <p>The <code>pdx-affix</code> component wraps any element and makes it stick to the top (or bottom) of the scroll container when the user scrolls past it.</p> <p>Here, inside a scroll container, it is CSS sticky: it keeps its own place in the flow, so nothing jumps.</p> <p>You can configure the offset from top/bottom and target a specific scroll container.</p> <p class="pdx-ink-muted">Keep scrolling...</p> <p>The state is reported by an IntersectionObserver rooted at the container — no scroll listener in this mode.</p> <p>When the user scrolls back up, the element returns to its normal flow position.</p> <p class="pdx-ink-muted">Almost there...</p> <p>End of scrollable content.</p> </div> </div> <details class="source-block"> <summary>Source</summary> <pre class="pdx-txt-mono"><code>&lt;div class="scroll-container" id="affix-container"&gt;\\n  …\\n  &lt;pdx-affix :offsetTop="0" target="#affix-container"\\n    @pdx-change="e =&gt; affixed = e.detail.affixed"&gt;\\n    &lt;div class="sticky-bar"&gt;Sticky Toolbar&lt;/div&gt;\\n  &lt;/pdx-affix&gt;\\n  …\\n&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre> </details> </section> '));
