const __blk0=staticBlock(staticMarkup(' <section> <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Live Demo</h2> <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll the content below. The nav links highlight automatically.</p> <div class="spy-layout"> <pdx-scroll-spy> <nav class="spy-nav" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <a class="spy-link" href="#spy-intro" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-intro" data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Introduction</a> <a class="spy-link" href="#spy-install" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-install" data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Installation</a> <a class="spy-link" href="#spy-usage" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-usage" data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Usage</a> <a class="spy-link" href="#spy-api" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-api" data-pdx-mgcxv-in>API Reference</a> <a class="spy-link" href="#spy-faq" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-faq" data-pdx-mgcxv-in>FAQ</a> </nav> <div class="spy-content" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <div class="spy-section" data-section="spy-intro" id="spy-intro" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <h3 data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Introduction</h3> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>ScrollSpy observes which section is currently in the viewport and highlights the corresponding navigation link. This is useful for long documentation pages, landing pages, and single-page navigation.</p> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>The component uses IntersectionObserver for efficient, performant section detection — no scroll event polling.</p> </div> <div class="spy-section" data-section="spy-install" id="spy-install" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <h3 data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Installation</h3> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Import the component from <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>@pdxui/ui</code>. It auto-registers as <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>&lt;pdx-scroll-spy&gt;</code>.</p> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Wrap your navigation links and content sections inside the component. Add <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>data-spy-link</code> to nav links and <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>data-section</code> to content sections.</p> </div> <div class="spy-section" data-section="spy-usage" id="spy-usage" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <h3 data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Usage</h3> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Place <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>data-spy-target="sectionId"</code> on each link to match the section\\'s <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>data-section</code> value. The component automatically adds an <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>active</code> class to the currently visible section\\'s link.</p> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Clicking a link scrolls smoothly to the target section (configurable via <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>smoothscroll</code> prop).</p> </div> <div class="spy-section" data-section="spy-api" id="spy-api" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <h3 data-pdx-mgcxv-in>API Reference</h3> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Configure the observation threshold with the <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>offset</code> prop. Customize selectors with <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>sectionselector</code> and <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>linkselector</code> props.</p> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in>The component emits a <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>pdx-change</code> event when the active section changes, with the section key in the event detail.</p> </div> <div class="spy-section" data-section="spy-faq" id="spy-faq" data-pdx-mgcxv-in> <h3 data-pdx-mgcxv-in>FAQ</h3> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in><strong data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Q: Does it work with dynamic content?</strong><br data-pdx-mgcxv-in>A: Yes, the observer watches for DOM mutations and re-initializes automatically.</p> <p data-pdx-mgcxv-in><strong data-pdx-mgcxv-in>Q: Can I use custom selectors?</strong><br data-pdx-mgcxv-in>A: Yes, use the <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>sectionselector</code> and <code data-pdx-mgcxv-in>linkselector</code> props.</p> </div> </div> </pdx-scroll-spy> </div> <details class="source-block"> <summary>Source</summary> <pre class="pdx-txt-mono"><code>&lt;pdx-scroll-spy&gt;\\n  &lt;nav&gt;\\n    &lt;a data-spy-link data-spy-target="intro"&gt;Intro&lt;/a&gt;\\n    &lt;a data-spy-link data-spy-target="usage"&gt;Usage&lt;/a&gt;\\n  &lt;/nav&gt;\\n  &lt;div data-section="intro" id="intro"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;\\n  &lt;div data-section="usage"